  "about": "Visible dev-only query set for the deterministic zoop-ai-graph tool baseline. It names WHAT to ask (version, anchor company, depth) and holds no expected answer; the hand-authored expectation lives in expected.json and is opened only by `score`. The world is synthetic: S1/S2/S3 authored replay (ai/pipeline/scripts graph_projection_smoke.py world plus the `split` job in graph_tool_bench.py `prepare`), projected into a throwaway Neo4j database. Company IDs are the canonical IDs the operator registry assigns to SYNTH-2 (kr-000050), SYNTH-1 (kr-000100), SYNTH-3 (kr-000300) and SYNTH-4 (kr-000400).",
  "versions": {
    "main": "S3 job rel-main: 7 eligible relations over all five projected types, one two-step indirect supply path, one symmetric pair, one event and one topic node.",
    "split": "S3 job rel-split: one INVESTS_IN edge and one COMPETES_WITH edge over four companies, two disconnected components."
  },
